infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Sawtooth vs staircase: provisioning or leak?
  desc The one diagnostic — does old space drop after a full GC? — that tells a tuning fix from a leak hunt
  compares
    - label Sawtooth: memory returns after a full GC
      children
        - label Old space drops sharply, then refills
          desc Allocate, collect, repeat — the working set is legitimately large
        - label Diagnosis: under-provisioned
          desc Not a leak — the live set just needs more room
        - label Fix: raise --max-old-space-size
          desc A provisioning knob, and here the right call
    - label Staircase: memory never returns
      children
        - label Barely drops: 1850 → 1845 MB
          desc Full GC reclaims almost nothing; old space climbs every cycle
        - label Diagnosis: a leak
          desc A reachable reference — cache, listener, global — keeps growing
        - label Fix: 3 snapshots, cut the retainer
          desc Raising the heap only delays OOM: 14h → 28h, same slope
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
